# bagart/telegram-bot-menu-module

Standalone Telegram Mini App "menu" module (`TgModuleContract` plugin) for the
telegram-bot-platform: SPA shell + Web API + chat registry + roles/grants +
resource registry, per RFC `docs/tasks/menu.md` (v2.7).

## CONTRACT FREEZE (D40 — Phase 0.5)

The cross-boundary surface is **frozen** as of task 04 and guarded by golden
fixtures (`tests/Fixtures/Wire/`):

- PHP contracts namespace `BAGArt\TelegramBotMenu\Contracts\` (incl. the
  `SettingsWriterContract` draft; implementation lands in task 05)
- DTO/enum namespaces `Manifest\` and `Support\` (`TgUiContext`, refs,
  `Envelope`, resource DTOs, `TgWebApiRoute`)
- Wire formats §27.6: HTTP envelope, session bearer key set, `startapp` ctx
  signing, ETag triple (`fingerprint:epoch:permHash`, D59), version token,
  cursor
- Chunk surface `ts/bridge.d.ts` (api: 1) incl. feature token union and
  `searchResources()` (D41/D48); dev harness `ts/bridge-mock.ts`

Any signature or wire-format change from here on requires an explicit RFC
delta PR referencing D40 and must update the golden fixtures in the same PR.
CI runs this gate as the `contract-freeze` job (`.github/workflows/tests.yml`
→ `vendor/bin/pest --testsuite menu-unit --filter=Wire`).

## Development

- Dev mode: PSR-4 mapped from the host root composer.json into `src/`;
  provider listed in host `bootstrap/providers.php`; module self-registers
  into `config('telegram.modules_providers')`.
- Test: `composer test` (or from host root: `vendor/bin/pest --testsuite menu-unit`).
- Prod mode wiring (composer.prod.json overlay) is intentionally deferred
  until this package is published to its VCS home.
